import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout>
  <h1>FAQ</h1>

  <h2>What frameworks are supported?</h2>

  <p>ISO 27001:2022, SOC 2, NIST CSF, and Essential Eight are seeded automatically. You can import additional frameworks via CSV in the Frameworks → Import page.</p>

  <h2>How do vendors access the questionnaire?</h2>

  <p>Vendors receive an email with a unique, opaque portal link (<code>/portal/&lt;token&gt;</code>). No account or login is required — the token in the URL is the authentication mechanism. Tokens expire after 30 days by default and can be revoked at any time.</p>

  <h2>Can I password-protect the portal?</h2>

  <p>Yes. When sending an assessment, set a portal password. The vendor must enter it before accessing the questionnaire. The password is bcrypt-hashed in the database.</p>

  <h2>How is scoring calculated?</h2>

  <p>Total score = compliant weighted scores divided by total possible weighted scores (0.0–1.0). Unscorable question types (Free Text, File Upload, etc.) and N/A responses are excluded from the denominator. Risk weights (Critical=10, High=6, Medium=3, Low=1) are configurable in Settings → Scoring.</p>

  <h2>Can I configure SSO?</h2>

  <p>Yes. Settings → SSO supports Microsoft Entra ID, Google Workspace, and any generic OIDC-compliant IdP. All client secrets are encrypted at rest. When SSO is enforced, a break-glass URL (<code>/login?break-glass=&lt;token&gt;</code>) provides emergency local login access.</p>

  <h2>How do I set up email?</h2>

  <p>Settings → Email. Enter your SMTP host, port, credentials, and from address. Use the "Test SMTP" button to verify. Works with SendGrid (SMTP relay), Mailgun, and any standard SMTP provider.</p>

  <h2>What happens when a vendor deletes an uploaded file?</h2>

  <p>Portal uploads are validated server-side and cannot be deleted by the vendor after submission. Before submission, the vendor can remove files and upload replacements.</p>

  <h2>How do recurring assessments work?</h2>

  <p>Set an assessment's recurrence to Quarterly or Annual. The cron job automatically clones the assessment, sends a new invitation, and schedules the next run. The <code>nextRunAt</code> field on the assessment controls the schedule.</p>

  <h2>What does the cron job do?</h2>

  <p>The <code>/api/cron/run</code> endpoint (secured with <code>CRON_SECRET</code>) runs:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Reminder emails (7 and 1 day before due)</li>
    <li>Overdue escalation emails to reviewers</li>
    <li>Certification and contract renewal expiry notices (30 and 7 day)</li>
    <li>Recurring assessment creation</li>
    <li>Audit log pruning (configurable retention)</li>
    <li>Email log pruning (configurable retention)</li>
    <li>Orphaned file sweep (cleans unreferenced storage files)</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>How do I back up?</h2>

  <ol>
    <li><strong>Database:</strong> <code>pg_dump</code> the PostgreSQL database</li>
    <li><strong>Files:</strong> Back up the <code>EVIDENCE_STORAGE_PATH</code> directory (local disk) or your S3/Azure bucket</li>
    <li><strong>Scripts:</strong> <code>scripts/backup.sh</code> (Linux/macOS) and <code>scripts/backup.ps1</code> (Windows) automate both</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Is there a demo?</h2>

  <p>The <code>prisma/seed-demo.ts</code> script creates 50 vendors with realistic assessment data. Run with <code>npx tsx prisma/seed-demo.ts</code> (add <code>--reset</code> to wipe first). Requires a running database.</p>

  <h2>Can I extend it?</h2>

  <p>The source is on <a href="https://github.com/mitchelljfranklin/mitch-risk">GitHub</a>. It's a standard Next.js 16 app with Prisma — extend templates, add question types, integrate with your SIEM, or build custom reports. The REST API (with Swagger docs at <code>/docs</code>) is the recommended integration point.</p>
</DocsLayout>
